slides.append(slide(2,'Recall: two ways to value dividends',grid('<h3>One-stage DDM · Gordon</h3>'+eq(r'P_0=\frac{D_1}{k_e-g}=\frac{D_0(1+g)}{k_e-g}')+'<p>One sustainable growth rate forever. A mature firm with stable payout and risk.</p>'+eq(r'k_e>g'),'<h3>Two-stage DDM</h3>'+eq(r'P_0=\sum_{t=1}^{N}\frac{D_t}{(1+k_e)^t}+\frac{P_N}{(1+k_e)^N}')+eq(r'P_N=\frac{D_{N+1}}{k_e-g_s}')+'<p>Forecast the first stage explicitly; use Gordon only when stable growth begins.</p>')+'<div class="note-box">Same valuation logic today. Replace dividends paid with cash available to equity.</div>'))
slides.append(slide(3,'Dividends paid ≠ cash available',f'<figure class="fcfe-history"><img src="data:image/png;base64,{img}" alt="Historical real dividends and earnings from the DCF2 course slides"><figcaption>Historical chart from DCF2, slide 10. Original source: Robert Shiller, Yale. Historical snapshot, not a current forecast.</figcaption></figure>'+grid('<h3>What do you notice?</h3><p>Earnings fluctuate much more than dividends. Managers smooth payouts.</p>','<h3>Our question</h3><p>How much <b>could</b> the firm distribute after investment and financing?</p><p><b>FCFE</b> measures that capacity; it is not a promise to pay. Retained cash must still be valued consistently.</p>')))
slides.append(slide(4,'Build the cash available to equity',eq(r'FCFE=NI+D\&A-CapEx-\Delta WC+\text{Net debt issued}')+grid('<h3>Change one decision</h3><p>Illustrative company · $m. Net income 100; depreciation 20.</p><label>Cash CapEx<input id="lab-capex" type="range" min="20" max="160" value="70"></label><label>Increase in noncash operating WC<input id="lab-wc" type="range" min="-20" max="40" value="15"></label><label>Net debt issued<input id="lab-debt" type="range" min="-40" max="50" value="5"></label>','<h3>Where did the earnings go?</h3><div id="cash-waterfall"></div>')+'<div class="note-box">An increase in working capital uses cash. Net debt issued = new borrowing − principal repaid. Borrowing increases current cash available, but does not by itself create value.</div>'))
slides.append(slide(5,'Profitable does not always mean distributable','<p class="lead">Same firm, two years. Which year can fund a cash distribution internally?</p><table class="fcf-result-table"><thead><tr><th>Source example · $m</th><th>Year 1</th><th>Year 2</th></tr></thead><tbody>'+''.join(f'<tr><td>{a}</td><td>{b}</td><td>{c}</td></tr>' for a,b,c in [('Net income','1,160','1,615'),('Depreciation','283','373'),('CapEx','1,481','2,029'),('Increase in WC','391','131'),('Net debt issued','−25','238')])+'</tbody></table>'+reveal('two-years',grid('<h3>Year 1</h3>'+eq(r'FCFE=1160+283-1481-391-25=-454')+'<p>Investment and repayment exceed earnings plus noncash add-backs.</p>','<h3>Year 2</h3>'+eq(r'FCFE=1615+373-2029-131+238=66')+'<p>A positive amount remains after reinvestment and net borrowing.</p>'))+'<p class="source-note">DCF2, Example 1. Teaching example, not a current company forecast.</p>'))
slides.append(slide(6,'Reinvestment: how much must equity fund?',grid('<h3>Start with actual financing</h3>'+eq(r'\text{Net CapEx}=CapEx-D\&A')+eq(r'ER=\text{Net CapEx}+\Delta WC-\text{Net debt issued}')+eq(r'FCFE=NI-ER'),'<h3>Or assume a stable debt ratio</h3>'+eq(r'd=\frac{D}{D+E}\quad\text{(book values)}')+eq(r'ER=(1-d)(\text{Net CapEx}+\Delta WC)')+'<p>Debt funds fraction <b>d</b> of reinvestment; equity funds the rest. Use this shortcut only when that financing policy holds.</p>')+'<div class="note-box">Actual net debt issuance and the debt-financed share are alternative ways to estimate reinvestment. Do not subtract both.</div>'))
slides.append(slide(7,'Growth has to be funded',grid('<h3>Equity reinvestment rate</h3>'+eq(r'ERR=\frac{ER}{NI}=1-\frac{FCFE}{NI}')+eq(r'g=ERR\times ROE')+'<p>With stable reinvestment, profitability and leverage, sustainable earnings growth carries through to FCFE.</p>','<h3>DCF2 · Example 2</h3><p>NI = 2,177; net CapEx = 468; increase in WC = 852; net debt issued = −104 ($m). ROE = 23.12%.</p>'+reveal('growth-answer',eq(r'ER=468+852-(-104)=1424')+eq(r'ERR=1424/2177=65.41\%')+eq(r'g=65.41\%\times23.12\%\approx15.12\%')))+'<div class="note-box">15.12% is an implied growth estimate, not automatically a defensible perpetual rate. A mature-stage forecast may require lower ROE or reinvestment.</div>'))
slides.append(slide(8,'FCFE gives equity value directly',eq(r'V_{E,0}=\frac{FCFE_1}{k_e-g}=\frac{FCFE_0(1+g)}{k_e-g}')+grid('<h3>Use the equity discount rate</h3>'+eq(r'k_e=r_f+\beta\,ERP')+'<p>Match equity cash flow with equity risk. Use normalized current FCFE and sustainable stable growth.</p>','<h3>From total value to one share</h3>'+eq(r'P_0=\frac{V_{E,0}}{\text{Shares outstanding}}')+'<p>Millions of dollars divided by millions of shares gives dollars per share.</p>')+'<div class="note-box">Require cost of equity above growth. Do not subtract debt again: financing is already reflected in FCFE. These examples assume no separately valued nonoperating assets.</div>'))
